# Normalize line endings so every platform checks out and stores LF, regardless
# of the host's core.autocrlf setting. Windows CI sets `core.autocrlf false`
# before checkout for the same reason (see .github/workflows/ci.yml): CRLF
# conversion breaks shell scripts and Go tooling that assume LF — notably
# `gofmt -l`, which flags every file it would rewrite when the working tree
# carries CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect text files and leave binary assets (images,
# archives, the ONNX library, the .onnx model) untouched. `eol=lf` pins the
# working-tree line ending to LF for the text files it detects. This makes LF
# canonical in the repository itself instead of relying on each contributor's
# local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
